    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d599">

                <pb facs="0572" n="560" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg560"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/965a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-02T18:00:00-05:00">October 2, 1939—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1134. Please inform the British Government that in view of the suspension of the
                    obligations of the London Naval Treaty, 1936, by several other parties to the
                    treaty and in accordance with article 24, <pb facs="0573" n="561" xml:id="pg561"
                    /> this Government suspends so far as it is concerned all the obligations of the
                    treaty.</p>
                <p>Request that notice to this effect be transmitted to the Governments of
                    Australia, New Zealand, and India.</p>
                <p>Similar notice is being given to other parties to the treaty.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
